    {
      "id": "1e88e449-6baf-41c9-9ee7-f23a3a6c4944",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "green",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "level": 3,
        "isToggleable": false
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Success Metrics / KPIs",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "57adc47a-925d-4e3e-a053-7dd78c366f65",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "How might you measure what success means to you? Think of these are your Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) — these are things you can measure that provide evidence that you are making progress towards your goals. For consumer-facing digital products, your goals might be user acquisition/retention, but they may also be quality measures such as number of positive responses, or project process things like code unit tests or PRs approved.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "b1b552dd-c50e-4f86-8563-0c5adb19f69b",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Your measurements may fall into two types: lagging measurements are things that have happened or outputs such as number of users and sales; leading measurements are inputs and processes such as code quality or signups that may predict future outputs. Think about desired outcomes such as behavior change/usage,",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "67d6d842-4171-40a0-ab36-a733bb64c096",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🕐 While we may not have enough time to get good measurements, thinking about what some measurements are that you could use will help you identify ways to evaluate your success and measure progress as well as use as a feedback mechanism for potential improvement.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
